{"path": "/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12858/comments", "params": {"per_page": 100}, "body": [{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/3955233710", "html_url": "https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12858#issuecomment-3955233710", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12858", "id": 3955233710, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBWBCuM7rwBOu", "user": {"login": "andresliszt", "id": 36001403, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDAxNDAz", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36001403?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/andresliszt", "html_url": "https://github.com/andresliszt", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andresliszt/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andresliszt/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andresliszt/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andresliszt/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andresliszt/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andresliszt/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andresliszt/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andresliszt/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/andresliszt/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-02-24T23:07:36Z", "updated_at": "2026-02-24T23:07:36Z", "body": "Not only with generics:\n\n```python\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nclass Foo(BaseModel):\n    x: BaseModel\n\n# Validation succeeds, but the resulting object is \"broken\"\nm = Foo(x={}) \n```\n\nLooking at #12859, does it make sense allowing `x = {}` for this particular pydantic model? If we allow `x = {}` it means we allow `x = BaseModel()`, which we know is not possible:\n\n`pydantic.errors.PydanticUserError: Pydantic models should inherit from BaseModel, BaseModel cannot be instantiated directly`\n\n", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/3955233710/reactions", "total_count": 1, "+1": 1, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/3957970098", "html_url": "https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12858#issuecomment-3957970098", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12858", "id": 3957970098, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBWBCuM7r6dSy", "user": {"login": "Viicos", "id": 65306057, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjY1MzA2MDU3", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65306057?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos", "html_url": "https://github.com/Viicos", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-02-25T09:34:37Z", "updated_at": "2026-02-25T09:34:37Z", "body": "Using `BaseModel` as an annotation or type var bound is a (unfortunately common) mistake. I believe users do it as they expect `BaseModel` subclasses to be provided. I'm not sure what would be the best way forward. It kind of makes sense to allow it if you provide actual `BaseModel` subclasses, but we should definitely prevent plain dicts to be provided.", "author_association": "MEMBER", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/3957970098/reactions", "total_count": 1, "+1": 1, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/3957973569", "html_url": "https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12858#issuecomment-3957973569", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12858", "id": 3957973569, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBWBCuM7r6eJB", "user": {"login": "Viicos", "id": 65306057, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjY1MzA2MDU3", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65306057?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos", "html_url": "https://github.com/Viicos", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Viicos/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-02-25T09:35:13Z", "updated_at": "2026-02-25T09:35:13Z", "body": "Tracking in https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/12861, which was transferred from pydantic-core.", "author_association": "MEMBER", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/3957973569/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 